stream
- id: T001
  title: "Create repository and planning contract"
  phase: "P0"
  state: "KA"
  depends_on: []
  files:
    - "README.md"
    - "AGENTS.md"
    - ".gitignore"
    - "LICENSE"
    - "docs/plan.pdf"
    - "docs/decisions.md"
  steps:
    - >-
      Create a new folder named monsoon-atlas; run git init. Preserve existing unrelated
      repositories.
    - >-
      Copy this PDF to docs/plan.pdf; record Karnataka -> Kerala -> Delhi, Rs0/no-card,
      real data, Python3.12 and DuckDB1.x constraints in AGENTS.md.
    - >-
      Use MIT for original code only; dataset licences remain separate. Ignore .env,
      .venv, data/raw, data/clean, secrets and mlruns.
  commands:
    - "git init"
    - "git check-ignore .env"
    - "git rev-parse --is-inside-work-tree"
  acceptance:
    command: "git rev-parse --is-inside-work-tree; git check-ignore .env"
    expected: >-
      git rev-parse --is-inside-work-tree prints true; required files exist; .env is
      ignored.
  hours: 1
- id: T002
  title: "Python 3.12 environment, linting and tests"
  phase: "P0"
  state: "KA"
  depends_on:
    - "T001"
  files:
    - "pyproject.toml"
    - "requirements/core.in"
    - "requirements/core.txt"
    - "requirements/dev.in"
    - "requirements/dev.txt"
    - "src/atlas/__init__.py"
    - "tests/test_environment.py"
  steps:
    - >-
      Install official Python3.12.10 x64 if absent; py -3.12 must resolve3.12,
      never3.14. Create venv.
    - >-
      Pin core: duckdb/httpx/pydantic/typer/PyYAML/pyarrow/pandas/numpy; dev:
      pytest/pytest-cov/ruff/pip-tools. Use section5 pins and compile hash locks on
      Windows.
    - >-
      Test Python major/minor, DuckDB major1, Parquet roundtrip and DB reopen integrity.
      Expose package with editable install. If pins conflict, test a compatible exact
      patch and record lock/ADR; no blind upgrades.
  commands:
    - "py -3.12 -m venv .venv"
    - ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pip install pip-tools==7.6.2"
    - >-
      .\.venv\Scripts\python -m piptools compile --generate-hashes requirements/core.in
      -o requirements/core.txt
    - ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pip install --require-hashes -r requirements/core.txt"
    - >-
      .\.venv\Scripts\python -m piptools compile --generate-hashes requirements/dev.in
      -o requirements/dev.txt
    - ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pip install --require-hashes -r requirements/dev.txt"
    - ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pip install --no-deps -e ."
    - ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pip check"
    - ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m ruff check ."
    - ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m ruff format --check ."
    - ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/test_environment.py -q"
  acceptance:
    command: ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/test_environment.py -q"
    expected: >-
      All tests pass; ruff check and format --check pass; pip check reports no broken
      requirements.
  hours: 3
- id: T003
  title: "Shared config, typed contracts and CLI"
  phase: "P0"
  state: "KA"
  depends_on:
    - "T002"
  files:
    - "src/atlas/config.py"
    - "src/atlas/contracts.py"
    - "src/atlas/cli.py"
    - "src/atlas/__main__.py"
    - "configs/states/ka.yaml"
    - "configs/budgets.yaml"
    - "tests/test_config.py"
  steps:
    - >-
      Define SourceConfig, FetchContext, RawArtifact, DatasetManifest and ModelRelease
      as specified in section4; reject unknown config keys.
    - >-
      Implement CLI skeleton ingest, validate, features, train, evaluate, publish,
      replay, audit and quota with --help. No empty successful commands: unimplemented
      commands exit2.
    - >-
      Set UTC storage, Asia/Kolkata display, budgets from section5, disabled-by-default
      unverified sources, and explicit input/output paths.
  commands:
    - ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/test_config.py -q"
  acceptance:
    command: ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/test_config.py -q"
    expected: >-
      Reject unknown source, bad CRS and paid-provider config; CLI help exits0;
      unsupported commands exit2.
  hours: 3
- id: T004
  title: "Fetch boundary and immutable raw ledger"
  phase: "P0"
  state: "KA"
  depends_on:
    - "T003"
  files:
    - "src/atlas/ingest/http.py"
    - "src/atlas/ingest/raw_store.py"
    - "src/atlas/ingest/base.py"
    - "tests/test_http.py"
  steps:
    - >-
      Implement fetch_bytes(ctx,url)->RawArtifact with allowlisted hosts, timeout30s,
      max3 retries2/8/30s+jitter, Retry-After and conditional GET.
    - >-
      SHA256 content-address every artifact; record fetched_at, provider-issued time
      separately, HTTP metadata without credentials. Atomic write temp then rename.
    - >-
      Implement offline fixture replay, max-byte limit, redirect allowlist and circuit
      breaker after3 consecutive failures.
  commands:
    - ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/test_http.py -q"
  acceptance:
    command: ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/test_http.py -q"
    expected: >-
      304 makes no duplicate;429 waits per header; interrupted write leaves prior data
      intact; secrets absent from logs.
  hours: 3
- id: T005
  title: "Schema registry and available-at-time joins"
  phase: "P0"
  state: "KA"
  depends_on:
    - "T004"
  files:
    - "src/atlas/data/validate.py"
    - "src/atlas/data/asof.py"
    - "schemas/common.json"
    - "tests/test_asof.py"
  steps:
    - >-
      Implement common envelope from section7 and contract versioning; preserve provider
      columns in mapping metadata.
    - >-
      asof_join uses available_at<=issue_at, valid time and revision version; preserve
      nulls and missing-reason enum.
    - >-
      Create tests from small documented real-record fixtures plus deliberately
      malformed copies for boundary testing. Never publish test fixtures as
      observations.
  commands:
    - ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/test_asof.py -q"
  acceptance:
    command: ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/test_asof.py -q"
    expected: >-
      Late revisions cannot enter past predictions; duplicate snapshots idempotent;
      midnight IST converted correctly; missing!=0.
  hours: 3
- id: T006
  title: "Versioned Parquet manifests and quota ledger"
  phase: "P0"
  state: "KA"
  depends_on:
    - "T005"
  files:
    - "src/atlas/data/store.py"
    - "src/atlas/data/manifest.py"
    - "src/atlas/data/budget.py"
    - "tests/test_storage.py"
  steps:
    - >-
      Partition by source/state/year/month; write Parquet target64MB shards, row
      groups16MB; hash every file. DuckDB is a rebuildable single-writer cache.
    - >-
      Publish manifest last; retain prior two manifests for rollback. Record byte budget
      and archive-only status at80%, stop new ingestion at95%.
    - >-
      Implement data_revision and published_at separately from observation time; never
      delete archived history automatically to meet quota.
  commands:
    - ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/test_storage.py -q"
  acceptance:
    command: ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/test_storage.py -q"
    expected: >-
      Failed upload leaves current manifest unchanged; quota stop preserves all existing
      snapshots; rebuild from Parquet equals original counts.
  hours: 3
- id: T007
  title: "Cross-platform CI and dependency audit"
  phase: "P0"
  state: "KA"
  depends_on:
    - "T006"
  files:
    - ".github/workflows/ci.yml"
    - "requirements/geo.in"
    - "requirements/ml.in"
    - "requirements/dl.in"
    - "scripts/audit_dependencies.py"
    - "tests/test_locks.py"
  steps:
    - >-
      Add Windows and Ubuntu Python3.12 jobs for core imports, lint and tests. Compile
      separate group locks with exact section5 versions; do not load torch in ingest
      jobs.
    - >-
      Audit direct/transitive dependencies and licences; capture registry release URL
      and Windows wheel availability. Resolve incompatibilities with a documented exact
      pin.
    - >-
      Pin GitHub Actions to audited commit SHA during implementation, minimal
      contents:read permissions, no secrets on fork PRs.
  commands:
    - ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/test_locks.py -q"
  acceptance:
    command: ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/test_locks.py -q"
    expected: >-
      All direct tools have exact locks; source-policy checker rejects secrets and
      unpinned paid services; both CI OS jobs green.
  hours: 3
- id: T008
  title: "Verify access, units and licence: KWRIS reservoirs and rainfall"
  phase: "P1"
  state: "KA"
  depends_on:
    - "T007"
  files:
    - "configs/sources/s28.yaml"
    - "docs/sources/s28.md"
    - "tests/fixtures/s28/manifest.json"
