      end-of-day level in metres and, separately if reported, storage in million cubic
      metres. Multi-output reports remain separate targets; labels S28.
    - >-
      Build feature table and feature provenance list from section11. Enforce data gate:
      >=5 years daily data, >=90% coverage and >=10 reservoirs for pooled learner.
      Monthly history cannot support these daily horizons. Level-only fallback if
      storage unavailable.
    - >-
      Write dated split manifest: Canonical prospective study: collect from 2028-01-17;
      train 2028-01-17..2028-03-28; tune 2028-03-29..2028-04-12; calibrate
      2028-04-13..2028-04-26; locked test 2028-04-27..2028-05-26. Expanding weekly
      folds; service-day and held-out route/station blocks; purge72h for M14, target
      horizon for other models. Dates assume source approval/readiness tasks pass on
      schedule. If delayed, shift the entire manifest before training; never invent
      earlier observations. Operational bias correction needs matched observed truth:
      train on historical data only if original issue-time forecasts exist; otherwise
      use this prospective window and keep raw weather as baseline. If evidence gate
      fails, write blocked evidence and stop this model branch; remaining model tasks
