- id: T153
  title: "Labels and features: Delhi bus arrival and delay"
  phase: "P4"
  state: "DL"
  depends_on:
    - "T034"
    - "T152"
    - "T149"
  files:
    - "configs/models/m12.yaml"
    - "src/atlas/features/m12.py"
    - "tests/models/test_m12_features.py"
  steps:
    - >-
      Implement target exactly: Vehicle-trip-stop prediction at each sampled position;
      target seconds until first observed stop arrival (within30m, dwell>=10s or crossed
      stop with interpolation gap<=120s); delay = observed arrival minus static GTFS
      scheduled arrival. Label source S38 only.
    - >-
      Build feature table and feature provenance list from section11. Enforce data gate:
      >=60 service days, >=20 routes and >=5000 matched completed stop arrivals;
      complete static trip links. Missing trip IDs: headway only, no fabricated delays.
    - >-
      Write dated split manifest: Canonical prospective study: collect from 2028-01-17;
      train 2028-01-17..2028-03-28; tune 2028-03-29..2028-04-12; calibrate
      2028-04-13..2028-04-26; locked test 2028-04-27..2028-05-26. Expanding weekly
      folds; service-day and held-out route/station blocks; purge72h for M14, target
      horizon for other models. Dates assume source approval/readiness tasks pass on
      schedule. If delayed, shift the entire manifest before training; never invent
      earlier observations. If evidence gate fails, write blocked evidence and stop this
      model branch; remaining model tasks only test disabled state.
  commands:
    - ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/models/test_m12_features.py -q"
  acceptance:
    command: ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/models/test_m12_features.py -q"
    expected: >-
      Target and lag assertions pass on real labelled fixture; future-data mutation
      rejected; blocked model exports no prediction.
  hours: 3
