  title: "Background web-push feasibility and privacy gate"
  phase: "P5"
  state: "ALL"
  depends_on:
    - "T183"
  files:
    - "docs/decisions/web-push.md"
    - "worker/src/push.ts"
    - "web/src/push.ts"
    - "tests/test_push_policy.py"
  steps:
    - >-
      Document conflict: background Web Push requires retaining subscription
      endpoints/keys, which are pseudonymous personal data under the strict
      no-personal-data rule.
    - >-
      Default feature disabled, local in-app watch notifications enabled. Implement only
      capability detection and explicit disabled reason.
    - >-
      Specify conditional design if owner later relaxes policy: consent, private
      encrypted subscriptions,30-day expiry, delete endpoint, batch send, no public repo
      storage. Do not enable without revised policy.
  commands:
    - ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/test_push_policy.py -q"
  acceptance:
    command: ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/test_push_policy.py -q"
    expected: >-
      With privacy_mode=no_personal_data, no subscription leaves device and backend
      rejects registration; feature catalogue reports conditional stretch.
  hours: 2
- id: T185
  title: "PMTiles city-layer build and serving test"
  phase: "P5"
  state: "ALL"
  depends_on:
    - "T166"
    - "T070"
  files:
    - "src/atlas/spatial/tiles.py"
    - ".github/workflows/tiles.yml"
    - "tests/test_tiles_build.py"
  steps:
    - >-
      Use Tippecanoe2.79.0 in Linux CI,verified source tag; clip city layers before
      tiling. Shard PMTiles archivev3 to<20MiB.
    - >-
      Validate random tile samples against clipped source geometries;retain
      attribution/confidence fields.
    - >-
      Test HTTP Range206 and CORS on actual no-card host; fallback to smaller GeoJSON if
      failed.
  commands:
    - ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/test_tiles_build.py -q"
  acceptance:
    command: ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/test_tiles_build.py -q"
    expected: >-
      Tiles preserve bounds/IDs;file cap and Range206 tested;no unlicensed source
      included.
  hours: 3
- id: T186
  title: "Terrain and globe interaction"
  phase: "P5"
  state: "ALL"
  depends_on:
    - "T185"
    - "T066"
    - "T068"
    - "T016"
  files:
    - "web/src/map/Terrain.tsx"
    - "web/src/map/Globe.tsx"
    - "tests/test_tiles.py"
  steps:
    - >-
      Enable MapLibre terrain/globe with attributed tile sources and available imagery
      date.
    - >-
      Respect reduced-motion and detect WebGL/low-memory failures;fall back to2D
      map/list.
    - >-
      Test world wrap,terrain exaggeration default1 and missing tile imagery;do not
      cache tiles for offline without permission.
  commands:
    - ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/test_tiles.py -q"
  acceptance:
    command: ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/test_tiles.py -q"
    expected: >-
      PMTiles random tile reads match source geometry; large-file budget enforced; WebGL
      failure shows accessible list.
  hours: 3
- id: T187
  title: "Flights, satellites, ships and earthquake overlays"
  phase: "P5"
  state: "ALL"
