# 1. Summary

MONSOON ATLAS | India regional intelligence platform | Planning-only handover | 4 November 2026

Build one shared, public platform that explains what is happening, what could happen next, and how previous predictions performed. Start with Karnataka, reuse the platform for Kerala, then add Delhi. This document is the specification for Claude Code; it contains no implementation of the project.

| Decision | Concrete plan |
|---|---|
| Budget | Rs 0, no credit card, no paid APIs or hosting. Free pages.dev address. Static data and predictions first; capped optional Workers backend. |
| First useful release | Karnataka map, weather, official alerts, price history, Place Lens, provenance, health badges and an honestly evaluated price-spike baseline. Model scores appear only after evidence gates pass. |
| Core design | Python 3.12, DuckDB 1.x, typed Parquet, versioned manifests; React/MapLibre map. Public historical subsets on Hugging Face where licensed, local archive fallback. |
| Scientific rule | Time and spatial holdouts; features available at issue time; strongest simple baseline; paired confidence intervals; publish failed experiments as research, not operational predictions. |
| Delivery | 20 ordered sections, source and schema catalogue, complete feature inventory, 20 model specifications, 50 fixed RAG gold questions plus numeric test design, task-by-task build plan and identical YAML appendix. |

Hard boundaries: no emergency-service claim; no fabricated live feeds or labels; no replica of KW Live branding. Weather/model outputs, official alerts and inferred information stay visibly distinct. An experimental low-risk route is not a guaranteed safe evacuation route.

Scope is intentionally large. Section 15 computes the schedule from task hours, 10 hours/week and 25% contingency. A working MVP comes before optional neural, orbital, news and globe features. Data collection and registration may extend calendar time independently of coding effort.

Read first: sections 2-5 for assumptions and architecture; section 16 for execution; Appendix B for blockers. Each gated feature remains visible as unavailable until its source, licence, labels and acceptance checks are satisfied.

# 2. Assumptions and answers to questions

| Item | Planning assumption / consequence |
|---|---|
| Questions | The owner explicitly skipped answers. These are assumptions, not claims about the laptop or the owner. |
| Hardware | Windows 10 x64; 8GB RAM; 4 CPU cores; no usable GPU; 60GB free disk. Limit DuckDB memory to2GB, threads2; streamed Parquet and raster windows. Fail storage preflight below20GB; reduce AOI, not data fidelity. |
| Availability | Laptop is not always on. Automated public summaries run on free hosted jobs; local training/backfills can resume. Continuous Delhi collection is conditional on measured Worker feasibility. |
| Time and skill | 10 focused hours/week; intermediate Python/SQL, beginner web/geospatial/DL. Schedule includes25% contingency, not free unlimited AI labour. Each task1-3 hours; long training/collection waits are separately identified. |
| Existing price project | Only handoff claims are known:26.5M records,2021-May2026,16-day warning,PR-AUC0.33 at prevalence0.04. Repository path, columns, splits, licence and Karnataka coverage remain unverified. |
| Accounts | Assume owner can register no-card free GitHub, Cloudflare, Hugging Face and data-provider accounts. Account creation, terms acceptance and keys are owner steps during execution; this planning task creates none. |
| Dates | Illustrative build start9 Nov2026. Historical datasets freeze at4 Nov2026; future collections in cards are preregistration proposals, never existing data. Rebase prospective windows if the schedule starts later. |
| Budget meaning | Existing laptop, electricity, internet and existing AI subscriptions are treated as already available. No new project expense; this does not promise Claude Code itself is free. |
| Source status | VERIFIED means source/service reported tested in supplied handoff on4 Nov2026, not independently re-tested here. Exact export, schema, licence, account access and usable history still require task evidence. Dataset-level unknowns are UNVERIFIED. |
| Retention | Every published normalized snapshot retained from project launch; not every provider pixel or all global traffic. Raw response retention7/30 days is distinct. Finite free storage cannot guarantee forever; archive-only mode pauses ingestion before capacity exhaustion. |

### Original names and zero-cost addresses

| Name | Available-sounding deployment address | Decision |
|---|---|---|
| Monsoon Atlas | monsoon-atlas.pages.dev | Working choice; broad enough for environment, mobility and prices. |
| Nila Signal | nila-signal.pages.dev | Short, distinct; regional emphasis. |
| Place Pulse India | place-pulse-india.pages.dev | Emphasizes places and change. |
| Groundcast India | groundcast-india.pages.dev | Emphasizes forecasts with evidence. |
| Statewise Lens | statewise-lens.pages.dev | Emphasizes comparison and explainability. |

These are proposed names and free subdomain patterns, not checked availability or trademark clearance. The repository task records a search before final branding. Do not register a paid domain. Do not reuse KW Live text, name, logo or visual identity.

# 3. Decisions log

| ID | Decision | Alternative | Reason |
|---|---|---|---|
| D01 | Shared state-configured monorepo | Three independent apps | Reuse contracts, UI and model evaluation; state adapters contain differences. |
| D02 | Static public product plus optional small Worker | Always-on FastAPI/PostGIS service | Precomputed predictions and file API fit no-card free hosting. |
| D03 | Parquet truth, DuckDB1.x rebuildable cache | DuckDB as sole raw archive | Immutable files survive cache corruption; single writer only. |
| D04 | Public HF data subsets; local full archive | Cloudflare R2 by default | Do not rely on a service requiring billing activation. HF public space is best-effort, not guaranteed. |
| D05 | Admin places + H3 analysis cells | Treat H3 cells as wards | Public identities need real boundaries; stable hex cells support analytical joins. |
| D06 | LightGBM/linear champions only after tests | Neural model for every target | Small data and free compute favour baselines; three bounded neural experiments demonstrate DL honestly. |
| D07 | Prospective forecast-vintage collection | Future observed weather in historical forecast tests | Prevents leakage; reanalysis-only experiments labelled hindcasts. |
| D08 | Cloudflare Workers AI with extractive fallback | Paid Claude API; assume Gemini fixed quota | 10k-neuron free cap is documented; choose a supported free model and fail closed if availability changes. |
| D09 | Immutable published snapshots + capacity stop | Infinite free archive promise | Finite quotas require bounded ingestion; history is preserved when capacity reached. |
| D10 | Local watches, public Telegram channels | Personal accounts/DM database | No personal data collection. Background web push is conditional and disabled. |
| D11 | Official-warning display; research risk layers | Emergency routing or operational flood authority | Risk scores cannot guarantee road or shelter safety. |
| D12 | Exact candidate pins + compatibility gate | Claim untested environment is verified | Versions checked against package registry; integrated locks/Windows wheels tested in execution. |
| D13 | Dated split protocols and failed-model reports | One inflated global accuracy number | Per-state, per-horizon, per-event evidence is the portfolio differentiator. |
| D14 | All source URLs discovered from real pages | Guess resource IDs/endpoints | Canonical schemas are our design, never claims about unseen upstream fields. |
| D15 | Minimal CSS and accessible linked list | Copy reference website appearance | Original muted teal/sand design and non-map equivalents. |
| D16 | No live scrape of blocked services required | Depend on NCRB/WRIS/groundwater/GDELT | Optional discovery tasks may document a blocker; core pipeline is independent. |

# 4. Architecture and file tree

```
Provider feeds / permitted downloads / official documents
       | fetch with quotas, timestamps, content hash
       v
Raw artifacts (local, short retention) + immutable metadata ledger
       | parser + schema + unit / geometry / licence validation
       v
Versioned clean Parquet + GeoParquet + selected raster assets
       | point-in-time joins; data_revision manifest
       +--> EDA / statistics / population overlays
       +--> time / spatial split --> baseline --> candidate --> gate
       |                                           |
       |                           immutable model + forecast vintages
       v                                           v
HF permitted archive + static JSON/PMTiles + latest manifest
       |                     |                     |
       v                     v                     v
React/MapLibre map      Accuracy / quality      City Memory replay
       |
       +--> Browser local watches / optional local embedding search
       +--> Worker: trusted-document retrieval -> capped LLM -> citations
       +--> Official public Telegram channel (no personal subscribers DB)

Optional Delhi Worker cron -> sampled snapshot blobs in D1
       -> daily validated Parquet export -> verified archive -> D1 purge
       -> fail closed if free CPU, source, privacy or size limits fail
```

### Module contracts

| Interface | Exact contract / owner |
|---|---|
| FetchContext | source_id:str, state:str, run_id:str, requested_at:UTC datetime, budget:Budget, raw_root:Path, secrets:ephemeral mapping. Owned by ingest/base.py. |
| RawArtifact | sha256:str, path:Path, fetched_at:UTC datetime, upstream_issued_at:datetime/null, media_type:str, response_status:int, source_url:str, schema_mapping_version:str. No secrets in serialization. |
| Adapter.fetch | fetch(ctx: FetchContext) -> list[RawArtifact]. parse(raw: RawArtifact, config: SourceConfig) -> pyarrow.Table. Disabled sources raise SourceUnavailable; never return synthetic rows. |
| Feature builder | build_features(model_id:str, issue_at:datetime, manifest:DatasetManifest) -> pyarrow.Table. Requires every constituent available_at<=issue_at; emits feature provenance JSON. |
| Model runner | fit(spec:ModelSpec, train:Table, tune:Table)->ModelArtifact; predict(model, features)->PredictionTable; evaluate(predictions, labels, baseline)->EvaluationReport. Test set never passed to fit. |
| Publish/replay | publish(manifest, artifacts)->release_id:str, atomic manifest-last. replay(place_id, as_of, mode) selects available_at<=as_of; mode is as_known or reconstructed. |
| Frontend API | GET /api/v1/current.json; /api/v1/snapshots/{snapshot_id}.json; /api/v1/models/{model_id}.json; optional POST /ask accepts query, language, place_id, as_of, chunk_ids; output answer, citations[], status. |
| CLI | python -m atlas ingest --source S01 --state ka --as-of ISO; validate --manifest PATH; features --model M06 --as-of ISO; train --model M06 --split PATH; evaluate --run ID; publish --manifest PATH; replay --place ID --as-of ISO; audit --scope all; quota --check. All errors exit nonzero. |

Naming: Python snake_case modules, PascalCase types, Sxx source IDs, Mxx model IDs, Fxxx features and Txxx tasks. State IDs ka/kl/dl; dates ISO8601; API schema_version integer; major changes require migration and old-reader test. Config is YAML; secret values are environment bindings, never YAML.

### Spatial identity and joins

Place ID: in:{state}:{kind}:{publisher_id}:{boundary_version}; separate stable_entity_id links successive boundary versions. kind is state/district/taluk/ward/facility/building/h3. Never derive identity solely from name. Alias crosswalk records source ID, canonical ID, match method, score, reviewer and validity dates. Address searches return a temporary point with accuracy, never a stored household ID; buildings use release+geometry hash, not owner identity.

Use EPSG:4326 for stored vector coordinates; EPSG:3857 only for map display. Compute local distances/areas in UTM43N EPSG:32643 for Kerala/west Karnataka and Delhi, or UTM44N EPSG:32644 for east Karnataka; choose by longitude. Statewide summaries use equal-area EPSG:6933. Geodesic radius checks avoid projection-edge distortion. H3 resolution7 for state aggregation,8 for city exploration; hexes are not flood-depth cells.

Point-to-admin joins use version-matched polygons. Raster-to-polygon aggregation uses fractional area coverage; population counts sum, intensive variables average with weights. Boundary crosswalks are many-to-many; show unmatched fraction. Municipal boundary and road network vintage must precede forecast time or be labelled static hindsight. Nearest facility is straight-line distance unless an explicit routable-network result exists.

Use local gazetteer search first. Optional Nominatim is user-triggered, <=1 request/second across app, identifying User-Agent, cached, no autocomplete or bulk geocoding. Its usage policy is https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/nominatim/. Any submitted address is transient; no query/location analytics.

