Dependencies grouped core/dev/geo/ml/dl/web; GPU torch installed only in a separate Colab/Kaggle notebook environment whose exact CUDA and wheel combination is recorded at run time. No cross-environment pickle loading. Browser and Python packages with the same name (pmtiles, playwright) have separate locks.

### Free tiers, budgets and zero-cost fallbacks

| Service | Provider limit / evidence | Project cap and fallback | Official reference |
|---|---|---|---|
| Cloudflare Pages | 500 builds/month,20000 files,25MiB/file; build timeout20min | Project<=120 builds/month,10000 files,20MiB/file. Static summary refresh daily; current data fetched separately. Fallback local static preview and permitted GitHub Pages evaluation. | https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/platform/limits/ |
| Cloudflare Workers Free | 100000 requests/day;10ms CPU/request;128MB;50 subrequests/request;5 cron triggers | Project<=20000 requests/day,2 cron triggers. No heavy dataframes/embeddings. Disable backend/live poll if CPU benchmark fails; static app still works. | https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/ |
| Workers AI | 10000 neurons/day; model eligibility varies; requests stop at cap on Free | Use <=8000 neurons/day and100 Ask requests/day, model token costs measured. Cited extractive retrieval if unavailable. Never upgrade or enable billing. | https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers-ai/platform/pricing/ |
| Cloudflare D1 Free | 5M rows read/day,100k rows written/day,5GB total; per-database constraints also apply | Budget<=100k reads/day,10000 writes/day,400MB database. One snapshot blob/tick, not one vehicle/row. Daily archival and7-day hot retention; stop before cap. | https://developers.cloudflare.com/d1/platform/pricing/ |
| Hugging Face public data | Best-effort public storage, no fixed guaranteed free allowance;100GB private allowance is not a public guarantee | Internal cap20GB public permitted artefacts,<=10000 files/repo, shards<=64MB. Local archive fallback; public latest summary stays small; request no paid expansion. | https://huggingface.co/docs/hub/en/storage-limits |
| GitHub Actions public repo | Standard hosted runner compute free for public repos; limits and fair-use apply; scheduled jobs may delay/disable | Budget daily10min pipeline +<=15min/hour bounded feed job only when useful; no endless live collectors. Artifacts<=400MB and7d retention; monthly owner checks schedule. Manual local command fallback. | https://docs.github.com/en/billing/concepts/product-billing/github-actions |
| Colab free GPUs | Dynamic allocation; not guaranteed; free sessions at most12h depending availability/usage | Stop/resume every2h; save checkpoint to existing local/permitted storage. CPU baselines and skipped neural challenger remain valid. Kaggle GPU quota/account verification is UNVERIFIED and optional, not assumed30h/week. | https://research.google.com/colaboratory/faq.html |
| Open-Meteo free service | Non-commercial; <10000 calls/day,5000/hour,600/minute; pricing lists300000/month | Project<=2000 weighted calls/day,200/hour,30/min,50000/month. Billable call weights vary with requested variables/time span; measure. Cache/drop optional grids when limit nears. | https://open-meteo.com/en/terms ; https://open-meteo.com/en/pricing |
| Other source APIs / tiles | No universal published quota established in handoff | Per-source local limits in catalogue are engineering caps, not provider promises. Source discovery records actual terms/quotas; unknown source stays capped or disabled. | Provider links in section6 |
| Rejected paid-risk choices | R2 free allocation does not establish no-card account eligibility; custom domains cost money; paid Claude API excluded | No R2, paid domains, paid inference, paid map services, paid OCR, paid GPU or billing-enabled trials in the required path. Gemini/Groq alternatives not relied on. | https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/pricing/ |

No free service provides a public-availability SLA. Owner creates accounts without billing activation; if signup demands a card, mark blocked and use the stated local/static fallback. A local fallback preserves the build, not a promise of equivalent public functionality. Record that distinction in the release report.

