### Shared ingestion profiles

| Profile | Rate cap | Retention / snapshots | Retries / gaps |
|---|---|---|---|
| daily | 1 request/5 seconds; 20/source/day initial cap | 30 days raw; immutable published records for project life | Null gaps; no label interpolation; retry 3 times at 2/8/30s + jitter; honour Retry-After |
| weather | Global Open-Meteo budget 2000 weighted calls/day, 200/hour, 30/minute; provider limits separately in section 5 | 30 days raw; retain every forecast vintage and published cell/date | Batch coordinates only if documented; reduce cells before quota; distinguish missing forecast and observation |
| fast | 1 request/5 seconds; max 96/source/day except approved hourly feeds | 30 days raw; retain every published change/version | Conditional GET; no update is not zero activity; stale badge after twice cadence |
| live | One upstream poll per configured region, at least 60s; adsb.lol at least 300s; provider quota overrides | 7 days full raw; every published selected-route snapshot retained; no full-state indefinite history | Shared cache; stop on quota; age badge; no GitHub cron claim of second-level reliability |
| bulk | 1 request/10 seconds; at most 2 download workers; 1 GB/day initial backfill throttle | Raw selected static release retained; newer releases do not erase historical versions used | Resume with checksum; manually approve parser changes; no filling unknown geography |
| tiles | On demand within provider policy; browser cache; no bulk prefetch | Store layer/date/URL manifest, not third-party tile pixels | No offline caching without explicit permission; base layer outage shows plain boundary outline |
| delivery | Public channel <=1 message/second and <=20/minute local cap; provider 429 wins | 90-day dedupe log; immutable content manifests | Queue limited to 100 messages/run; collapse repeats; no emergency delivery guarantee |

Every source uses HTTPS certificate verification,30s timeout, checksum, media type, retrieval timestamp and provider publication time when supplied. Generic dates without timezone are interpreted from documented publisher convention, never guessed. Store timezone-aware UTC; display/aggregate civil days in Asia/Kolkata (UTC+05:30). Daily calendar dates remain date types with timezone metadata. Raw source CRS is recorded; canonical vectors use EPSG:4326.

### Source-specific parsing, checks and storage sizing

| Source | Parser / profile | Validation and gap rule | Estimated footprint |
|---|---|---|---|
| S01 | JSON; weather | Rain >=0; humidity 0..100; forecast issue time known; units explicitly requested. | 0.50 GB/year |
| S02 | JSON; weather | Do not call reanalysis observations or assume it existed at forecast time; preserve release lag. | 1.0 GB backfill |
| S03 | JSON; weather | Missing river cells remain null; discharge >=0; this is model output, not a gauge. | 0.20 GB/year |
| S04 | JSON; weather | Pollutants >=0; never label CAMS a CPCB observation; preserve issue and valid times. | 0.20 GB/year |
| S05 | JSON; weather | Discover actual member count per product; do not hardcode the handoff estimate of 40. | 0.60 GB/year |
| S06 | JSON; weather | Record supported scenario and bias adjustment; not a weather forecast for an individual day. | 0.50 GB one-off |
| S07 | JSON; bulk | Decode fill values; verify units before conversion; do not silently combine products. | 0.20 GB |
| S08 | NetCDF or published binary via imdlib; bulk | Check actual file format and dimensions; imdlib may download binary grids, not NetCDF. Convert to NetCDF/Zarr only after parsing. | 1.5 GB state subsets |
| S09 | RSS/XML + CAP links; fast | CAP updates/cancellations supersede old alerts; missing geometry stays area text; do not infer lightning from rain. | 0.15 GB/year |
| S10 | JSON; live | Stale positions hidden after 5 minutes; no trajectory prediction beyond supplied data; no aircraft-owner enrichment. | 0.30 GB/year sampled |
| S11 | JSON; live | Discover current API credits and licence; disable rather than bypass a quota. | Included in S10 |
| S12 | TLE text; bulk | TLE checksum and epoch; extrapolated positions are inferred; hide elements older than 7 days. | 0.03 GB/year |
| S13 | WMTS XML and raster tiles; tiles | Select available date, not assumed today; clouds are not missing feed; imagery date visible. | 0.01 GB manifests; tiles on demand |
| S14 | PNG raster tiles; tiles | Decode Terrarium as R*256+G+B/256-32768 metres; validate sea-level samples. | 0.01 GB manifests |
| S15 | Style JSON + vector tiles; tiles | Retain OSM and OpenMapTiles attribution; check style and tile availability. | No stored tile archive |
| S16 | GeoTIFF; bulk | Conserve population sums during clipping; counts vs density must be distinguished; no individual records. | 0.80 GB state subsets |
| S17 | GeoJSON; bulk | No assumption 736 is current; valid polygons; preserve version and disputed-boundary metadata. ADM2 does not establish ward or taluk coverage. | 0.10 GB |
| S18 | PBF; bulk | Unique type/id/version; valid geometry; do not infer shelter opening status from OSM. | 2 GB clipped static; replaceable downloads |
| S19 | CSV gzip / WKT; bulk | Deduplicate within release; confidence 0..1; no ownership or inferred residents; >=0.75 display default. | 0.80 GB clipped city subsets |
| S20 | JSON; fast | Deduplicate by event ID and update time; distinguish preliminary magnitude. | 0.02 GB/year |
| S21 | JSON; bulk | Old schedules shown as historical reference, never current ETAs; pin commit hash. | 0.03 GB |
| S22 | JSON; daily | 0<min<=modal<=max; names mapped through versioned crosswalk; arrivals unit must be documented. | 2 GB existing history +0.15 GB/year |
| S23 | JSON; daily | Pagination counts, date parse, late reports; do not hardcode an invented resource UUID. | Included in S22 |
| S24 | JSON; fast | Validate station vs model; retain pollutant averaging interval; hourly snapshots may be rolling averages, not instantaneous truth. | 0.30 GB/year |
| S25 | JSON; fast | Deduplicate satellite/acquisition/location; hotspot is not confirmed building fire; report detection latency. | 0.05 GB/year |
| S26 | WebSocket JSON; live | Terms and websocket quotas unverified; no coastal coverage assumption; disable if unavailable. | 0.10 GB/year capped |
| S27 | HTML / documented JSON; fast | Counter reset vs interval rainfall; station moves/version; coverage >=80% per day. | 0.25 GB/year |
| S28 | HTML / official exports; daily | FIRST feasibility check: historical span and units. Never derive inflow from level alone; no implicit zero. | 0.03 GB/year |
| S29 | CSV / XLSX export; bulk | Reconcile station/hobli aggregation; do not mix duplicate gauges with S27. | 0.20 GB |
| S30 | GTFS ZIP/CSV; bulk | calendar exceptions; GTFS times above 24:00; stop coordinates; feeds not proof of live GPS. | 0.20 GB/year |
| S31 | HTML via Playwright if necessary; bulk | Exclude names/phones of individuals; geocode precision visible; no CAPTCHA bypass. | 0.05 GB/year |
| S32 | HTML; daily | Verify 16-dam list and units, datum and update date; no date inferred from fetch time. | 0.01 GB/year |
| S33 | JavaScript links / PDF or spreadsheet; bulk | Unknown archive depth; monthly labels do not support daily seven-day evaluation. | 0.05 GB |
| S34 | PDF; daily | Sample-check all columns and date; require manual review for OCR before model use. | 0.20 GB/year raw |
| S35 | Dataset-dependent; bulk | Handoff names a dataset family only. Must find dated location-level labels; aggregate annual rain table cannot validate a ward classifier. | 0.10 GB |
| S36 | PDF; bulk | Use district totals only at district resolution; no invented ward truth. | 0.05 GB |
| S37 | Research GIS files / PDF; bulk | Atlas maps are not necessarily reusable geospatial labels; unknown occurrence dates exclude temporal scoring. | 0.10 GB |
| S38 | GTFS ZIP + GTFS-realtime protobuf; live | Vehicle timestamps; map matching <=100m; trip/calendar match; no trip_id means no scheduled delay label. | 16 GB/year normalized sampled routes |
| S39 | HTTPS JSON; delivery | Public channels only; no subscriber/chat history collection; retry 429 per retry_after. | 0.01 GB/year |
| S40 | GeoJSON / GIS file; bulk | No guessed ward IDs or area boundaries; use district or H3 view until official geography is available. | 0.10 GB |
| S41 | RSS / permitted HTML; fast | No full-text republication by default; no victims names; original date not scrape date; preliminary marker required. | 0.05 GB/year |
| S42 | COG / SAFE; bulk | Sentinel-1 cannot yield NDVI. Use Sentinel-2 red/NIR with cloud mask for NDVI; SAR terrain correction and co-registration required. | 4 GB selected scenes; local only |
| S43 | Official GIS/CSV/PDF; bulk | OSM shelter tag cannot prove an open relief camp. No evacuee records; no ward labels fabricated from rainfall. | 0.05 GB |
| S44 | Official tables; bulk | Published totals only; no names or case locations; harmonize boundaries, under-reporting caveat. | 0.01 GB |

Row deduplication key is (source_id, natural_entity_id, valid_at, upstream_revision_or_content_hash). Re-fetching identical content changes fetch-log only; revisions create a new known_at version. Daily aggregations require>=80% expected samples and carry coverage; otherwise null. Fill short feature gaps only with trailing methods fitted on training data; flags and gap age are features. Labels are never interpolated. Source-specific exceptions in model cards override generic coverage rules.

### Storage arithmetic and retention boundary

| Store | Planning envelope | How capacity is enforced |
|---|---|---|
| Local60GB disk | 20GB immutable published archive +10GB permitted raw/static subsets +5GB working/raster cache +5GB model/env artifacts +20GB headroom | Measure first7 days and reforecast monthly. Keep at least20GB free; cap selected building/imagery AOIs. No full-India raster or global building download. |
| Public HF internal20GB cap | Tabular/history3GB + selected static layers2GB + forecast/model releases2GB + up to12GB sampled transit/year +1GB margin | Transit example:250 vehicles*960 ticks/day*50 compressed bytes=12MB/day,4.38GB/year;16GB/year is conservative cap including fields/overhead. Measure actual bytes, never rely on assumed compression. |
| D1 hot400MB | <=40MB normalized transit/day *7days=280MB plus metadata; per-row blob<=1MB | Do not write5000 vehicle rows each minute. Store one compressed selected-route snapshot/tick,<=960 ticks/day (16h). Export/verify before purge. If compressed size exceeds cap, reduce selected routes/cadence prospectively. |
| Pages assets | <=200MB deployment target;<=20MiB per file;<=10000 files | PMTiles city shards and small JSON; no forecast rebuild every minute. Archive references link to pinned HF revisions when permitted. |
| Long-term memory | No claim of unlimited lifetime storage | At80% warn and reduce future capture cadence with manifest annotation; at95% switch archive-only/read-only. Existing published snapshots survive; gaps and paused periods are explicit. |

City Memory captures what this product published and knew after launch. A2018 reconstruction uses documented historical data and is labelled reconstructed; it cannot claim to reproduce a system that did not exist then. Third-party tile images loaded directly by a browser are not ingested snapshots; their layer/date metadata is archived, and imagery unavailability is shown.

# 7. Data schemas

These are proposed normalized contracts, not invented upstream API fields. Each adapter task must record observed provider-field-to-contract mapping. Types are Arrow/Parquet: str UTF8, float float64, int int64, bool boolean, date date32, timestamp UTC microseconds, wkb binary with GeoParquet CRS metadata. ? denotes nullable. All sources inherit the following envelope; source tables below list additional fields.

| Common field | Type | Meaning / test |
|---|---|---|
| source_id / state | str / str | Sxx and ka/kl/dl/all; source registry foreign key. |
| record_id / snapshot_id | str / str | SHA256 natural key+provider revision; immutable published snapshot identifier. |
| observed_at / valid_at | timestamp? / timestamp? | Measurement/event time and time represented; timeless static assets may have nulls with reason. |
| issued_at / available_at | timestamp? / timestamp | Provider issue if documented; earliest time pipeline had usable record. Historical release unknown -> reconstructed flag. |
| fetched_at / published_at | timestamp / timestamp? | HTTP retrieval and product publication; never substituted for observation time. |
| source_url / raw_sha256 | str / str | Actual retrieved URL, excluding secrets; raw or original asset content hash. |
| schema_version / mapping_version | int / str | Contract major version and upstream parsing mapping revision. |
| provenance / quality_flags | enum / list[str] | official/model/inferred/reconstructed; flags e.g. missing,stale,imputed,unit_unverified. |
| licence_id / redistribution_allowed | str / bool | Explicit permission record; default false until reviewed. |
| place_id / boundary_version | str? / str? | Versioned geographic join; unmatched remains null, not guessed. |

