| Target / label / horizon / unit | 100m terrain cell; relative susceptibility to mapped slope failure, not a daily probability or trigger warning. Inventory S37, absence sampling only in surveyed footprint. |
| Features and lag evidence | S14 slope/aspect/elevation; terrain roughness and drainage proximity S18; antecedent climatology S08 prior to inventory event; no post-event land cover or event footprints as predictors. |
| Train / tune / calibration / test and CV | Train dated events through 2016; tune 2017; locked test 2018. If only 2018 inventory exists: 5 spatial catchment-block folds within 2018, report spatial validation only and no temporal-generalization claim. |
| Baselines | Slope-only logistic regression and inventory-density reference. |
| Candidate ladder / provisional final choice | Logistic and random forest versus LightGBM; default random forest for nonlinear terrain. |
| Metrics and release targets | PR-AUC >=1.20x same-sampling baseline; ROC-AUC secondary; recall at top 10% mapped area; bootstrap by event and spatial block. |
| Data feasibility gate | >=200 independent landslides with positional error <=100m and survey footprint; absence label sensitivity at 1:1/1:5/1:10 sampled controls. |
| Uncertainty / imbalance / explanations | Apply R/C/A shared protocol for the stated problem. Classes use training-only weights; regression has no class balancing. M09 presence-background outputs are relative scores; M10 clustered CI; M17 event-level bootstrap; M20 inherits base uncertainty, no new truth. |
| Failure modes | Survey bias and positional uncertainty; recalibration cannot turn presence-background scores into absolute risk. |
