Each implementation week holds at most8 task hours, leaving at least2 of the assumed10 hours for contingency and learning. Some space is intentionally unused because a task is not split across sessions. Collection-only weeks are genuine waits for future outcomes, not work that can be accelerated by writing code.

| Canonical study | Train | Tune / calibrate | Locked test |
|---|---|---|---|
| news | 2027-10-18..2027-12-16 | 2027-12-17..2028-01-15 / 2028-01-16..2028-01-30 | 2028-01-31..2028-02-14 |
| delhi | 2028-01-17..2028-03-28 | 2028-03-29..2028-04-12 / 2028-04-13..2028-04-26 | 2028-04-27..2028-05-26 |

These dates are generated from the same task schedule used in model cards and task instructions. Collection begins after its permission/readiness task finishes. Delhi evaluation waits until the locked test ends plus72-hour target maturation. If account access or source history is delayed, shift the full study and dependent schedule together before fitting; preserve the frozen old manifest as a superseded proposal. No backdated GPS or fictitious samples. Annotation tasks account for1000 real news articles and100 real anomaly reviews, including declared human time.

Critical path: Python/contracts -> KWRIS feasibility first -> core data/source rights -> place identity -> time-safe features -> price baseline -> Karnataka MVP -> remaining KA contracts/model gates -> Kerala history/label audit -> Kerala release -> Delhi approval and >=90-day capture -> frozen evaluation -> public forecast claims. Data history, redistribution permission and labels are the dominant risks; adding model complexity does not fix them.

| Risk | Likelihood / impact | Mitigation and fallback | Owner task |
|---|---|---|---|
| Daily reservoir history absent | High / high | Check KWRIS first; keep levels/history display; monthly archive cannot become daily labels. | T008 |
| Flood negatives or ward polygons missing | High / high | Coarser observed geography or exposure index; classifier disabled until independent labels. | T089 |
| 2018 labels only / hindsight | High / high | Descriptive replay; pre2018 training required for prospective-style claim. | T133 |
| Delhi OTD approval delayed | Medium / high | Start registration at Delhi phase; scheduled transit only; shift collection/test dates. | T152 |
| Free Worker CPU/size limit | High / high | Benchmark actual protobuf; sample smaller approved scope; active-view or owner-run capture; disable continuous ETA claims. | T152 |
| Free storage/rate cap exceeded | Medium / high | 80% warning,95% archive-only; local copy and smaller future sampling; never pay or silently erase history. | T006 |
| Source licence forbids reuse | High / high | Source permissions gate; link-only metadata or no ingestion; no public raw export. | T023 |
| Model fails simple baseline | High / medium | Publish baseline and failure analysis; portfolio values honest comparison. | T034 |
| LLM hallucinates / quota exhausted | Medium / high | Trusted retrieval, citation/numeric checks, fixed eval; extractive fallback. | T181 |
| Privacy conflict with push | Certain / medium | Disabled by default; local alerts and public channels. | T184 |
| Dependency or Windows wheel failure | Medium / medium | Exact compatibility locks and isolated geo/DL environments; tested replacement ADR. | T007 |
| Student time / large scope | High / high | MVP first,10h/week planning assumption,3h task cap, stretch can stay deferred with evidence. | T046 |
| Hazard route mistaken for official advice | Medium / high | No safety guarantee, verified shelter gate, official sources prominent; disconnected/stale returns unavailable. | T143 |
| Provider pages change or scraping blocked | High / medium | Fixture contracts, bounded retry, circuit breaker; no bypass; source-specific disabled status. | T004 |

# 16. Task list for Claude Code

Execution contract: read sections2-7 and the relevant model/feature card, select the earliest dependency-ready task, implement only its files/interfaces, run its acceptance command, record real outcome, then commit. The userâ€™s requested planning-only boundary ends here: this document supplies commands for the later coding agent; they were not executed against a project during planning. Public deployment and account setup belong to those implementation tasks.

Every task has ID,title,phase,state,depends_on,files,steps,commands,acceptance,hours. These same objects generate Appendix A, so the lists cannot drift. A passing disabled-source test means the fallback behaves correctly, not that the unavailable source/model is delivered. Keep blocked model tasks as evidence records; do not fabricate data to make them green.

Common task loop: write a meaningful failing test for the stated behaviour; implement minimal code; run the exact test and relevant regression suite; record evidence in the task log. Use real small source fixtures where allowed; deliberately malformed copies are test-only and never published as data. Formatting/lint checks are not substitutes for data/model acceptance.

### P0 - Repository and shared contracts

### T001 - Create repository and planning contract

Phase P0 | State KA | Depends on none | Estimate 1 hours

Files: README.md; AGENTS.md; .gitignore; LICENSE; docs/plan.pdf; docs/decisions.md

1. Create a new folder named monsoon-atlas; run git init. Preserve existing unrelated repositories.

2. Copy this PDF to docs/plan.pdf; record Karnataka -> Kerala -> Delhi, Rs0/no-card, real data, Python3.12 and DuckDB1.x constraints in AGENTS.md.

3. Use MIT for original code only; dataset licences remain separate. Ignore .env, .venv, data/raw, data/clean, secrets and mlruns.

```
git init
git check-ignore .env
git rev-parse --is-inside-work-tree
```

Acceptance command: git rev-parse --is-inside-work-tree; git check-ignore .env

Expected result: git rev-parse --is-inside-work-tree prints true; required files exist; .env is ignored.

### T002 - Python 3.12 environment, linting and tests

Phase P0 | State KA | Depends on T001 | Estimate 3 hours

Files: pyproject.toml; requirements/core.in; requirements/core.txt; requirements/dev.in; requirements/dev.txt; src/atlas/__init__.py; tests/test_environment.py

1. Install official Python3.12.10 x64 if absent; py -3.12 must resolve3.12, never3.14. Create venv.

2. Pin core: duckdb/httpx/pydantic/typer/PyYAML/pyarrow/pandas/numpy; dev: pytest/pytest-cov/ruff/pip-tools. Use section5 pins and compile hash locks on Windows.

3. Test Python major/minor, DuckDB major1, Parquet roundtrip and DB reopen integrity. Expose package with editable install. If pins conflict, test a compatible exact patch and record lock/ADR; no blind upgrades.

```
py -3.12 -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\python -m pip install pip-tools==7.6.2
.\.venv\Scripts\python -m piptools compile --generate-hashes requirements/core.in -o requirements/core.txt
.\.venv\Scripts\python -m pip install --require-hashes -r requirements/core.txt
.\.venv\Scripts\python -m piptools compile --generate-hashes requirements/dev.in -o requirements/dev.txt
.\.venv\Scripts\python -m pip install --require-hashes -r requirements/dev.txt
.\.venv\Scripts\python -m pip install --no-deps -e .
.\.venv\Scripts\python -m pip check
.\.venv\Scripts\python -m ruff check .
.\.venv\Scripts\python -m ruff format --check .
.\.venv\Scripts\python -m pytest tests/test_environment.py -q
```

Acceptance command: .\.venv\Scripts\python -m pytest tests/test_environment.py -q

Expected result: All tests pass; ruff check and format --check pass; pip check reports no broken requirements.

### T003 - Shared config, typed contracts and CLI

Phase P0 | State KA | Depends on T002 | Estimate 3 hours

Files: src/atlas/config.py; src/atlas/contracts.py; src/atlas/cli.py; src/atlas/__main__.py; configs/states/ka.yaml; configs/budgets.yaml; tests/test_config.py

