### T006 - Versioned Parquet manifests and quota ledger

Phase P0 | State KA | Depends on T005 | Estimate 3 hours

Files: src/atlas/data/store.py; src/atlas/data/manifest.py; src/atlas/data/budget.py; tests/test_storage.py

1. Partition by source/state/year/month; write Parquet target64MB shards, row groups16MB; hash every file. DuckDB is a rebuildable single-writer cache.

2. Publish manifest last; retain prior two manifests for rollback. Record byte budget and archive-only status at80%, stop new ingestion at95%.

3. Implement data_revision and published_at separately from observation time; never delete archived history automatically to meet quota.

```
.\.venv\Scripts\python -m pytest tests/test_storage.py -q
```

Acceptance command: .\.venv\Scripts\python -m pytest tests/test_storage.py -q

Expected result: Failed upload leaves current manifest unchanged; quota stop preserves all existing snapshots; rebuild from Parquet equals original counts.

