- id: T089
  title: "Labels and features: Bengaluru ward flood occurrence"
  phase: "P2"
  state: "KA"
  depends_on:
    - "T034"
    - "T078"
    - "T086"
    - "T031"
  files:
    - "configs/models/m01.yaml"
    - "src/atlas/features/m01.py"
    - "tests/models/test_m01_features.py"
  steps:
    - >-
      Implement target exactly: Ward x issue day; probability of >=1 independently
      documented inundation in the next 24 h. Negatives require a monitored ward-day
      with explicit coverage, not missing reports. Labels S43; horizon 24 h.
    - >-
      Build feature table and feature provenance list from section11. Enforce data gate:
      >=3 monsoons, >=100 positive ward-days across >=10 events, valid ward polygons and
      audited negatives. Otherwise publish rainfall exposure index, explicitly
      non-probabilistic.
    - >-
      Write dated split manifest: Train 2017-01-01..2022-12-31; tune
      2023-01-01..2023-06-30; calibrate remaining 2023; test 2024. Rolling monsoon-year
      origins; 5 spatial ward blocks with no shared event in training/test. If evidence
      gate fails, write blocked evidence and stop this model branch; remaining model
      tasks only test disabled state.
  commands:
    - ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/models/test_m01_features.py -q"
  acceptance:
    command: ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/models/test_m01_features.py -q"
    expected: >-
      Target and lag assertions pass on real labelled fixture; future-data mutation
      rejected; blocked model exports no prediction.
  hours: 3
- id: T090
  title: "Baseline and bounded candidate: Bengaluru ward flood occurrence"
  phase: "P2"
  state: "KA"
  depends_on:
    - "T089"
  files:
    - "src/atlas/models/m01.py"
    - "notebooks/models/m01.ipynb"
    - "tests/models/test_m01_fit.py"
  steps:
    - >-
      Fit baseline: Training ward-season prevalence; rain-threshold rule selected on
      validation. Save predictions on identical fold rows.
    - >-
      Fit candidate: Logistic regression, random forest, then LightGBM classifier;
      provisional LightGBM only after release gate. Use section11 search space and
      maximum30 CPU trials/2h; neural jobs use explicit N-card and resume checkpoints.
    - >-
      Save MLflow run, preprocessing, weights and split hashes; training function
      receives only train/tune data, never test. If blocked, preserve no-model manifest.
  commands:
    - ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/models/test_m01_fit.py -q"
  acceptance:
    command: ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/models/test_m01_fit.py -q"
    expected: >-
      Deterministic train smoke test passes; test rows cannot affect fit; all evaluated
      baselines have same target units and rows.
  hours: 3
- id: T091
  title: "Evaluate and publish decision: Bengaluru ward flood occurrence"
  phase: "P2"
  state: "KA"
  depends_on:
    - "T090"
  files:
    - "reports/models/m01.md"
    - "models/registry/m01.json"
    - "tests/models/test_m01_gate.py"
  steps:
    - >-
      Evaluate locked test once; report PR-AUC >=1.25x prevalence AND paired improvement
      over strongest baseline; Brier <=0.95x baseline; report ROC-AUC, F1, recall at <=5
      alerts/100 ward-days, ECE <=0.05.
    - >-
      Inspect failure modes: Under-reporting, changed drains, unmatched ward boundaries
      and urban rain cells; no house-level flood depth. Include source coverage,
      intervals, sliced performance and limits; block non-supported claims.
    - >-
      Export champion predictions/SHAP/intervals only if all gates pass; else publish
      baseline/research-only status. Save model card and retraining rule.
  commands:
    - ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/models/test_m01_gate.py -q"
  acceptance:
    command: ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/models/test_m01_gate.py -q"
    expected: >-
      Release manifest verifies source/split hashes and gate decision; failing model
      remains disabled; report never substitutes targets for achieved scores.
  hours: 3
- id: T092
  title: "Labels and features: Karnataka reservoir level and storage"
  phase: "P2"
  state: "KA"
  depends_on:
    - "T034"
    - "T027"
    - "T052"
  files:
    - "configs/models/m02.yaml"
    - "src/atlas/features/m02.py"
    - "tests/models/test_m02_features.py"
  steps:
    - >-
      Implement target exactly: Reservoir x daily issue x horizon {7,30} days;
      end-of-day level in metres and, separately if reported, storage in million cubic
      metres. Multi-output reports remain separate targets; labels S28.
    - >-
      Build feature table and feature provenance list from section11. Enforce data gate:
      >=5 years daily data, >=90% coverage and >=10 reservoirs for pooled learner.
      Monthly history cannot support these daily horizons. Level-only fallback if
      storage unavailable.
    - >-
      Write dated split manifest: Canonical prospective study: collect from 2028-01-17;
      train 2028-01-17..2028-03-28; tune 2028-03-29..2028-04-12; calibrate
      2028-04-13..2028-04-26; locked test 2028-04-27..2028-05-26. Expanding weekly
      folds; service-day and held-out route/station blocks; purge72h for M14, target
      horizon for other models. Dates assume source approval/readiness tasks pass on
      schedule. If delayed, shift the entire manifest before training; never invent
      earlier observations. Operational bias correction needs matched observed truth:
      train on historical data only if original issue-time forecasts exist; otherwise
      use this prospective window and keep raw weather as baseline. If evidence gate
      fails, write blocked evidence and stop this model branch; remaining model tasks
      only test disabled state.
  commands:
    - ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/models/test_m02_features.py -q"
  acceptance:
    command: ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/models/test_m02_features.py -q"
    expected: >-
      Target and lag assertions pass on real labelled fixture; future-data mutation
