- id: T130
  title: "Labels and features: Kerala seven-day dam forecast"
  phase: "P3"
  state: "KL"
  depends_on:
    - "T034"
    - "T129"
    - "T114"
    - "T116"
    - "T118"
  files:
    - "configs/models/m07.yaml"
    - "src/atlas/features/m07.py"
    - "tests/models/test_m07_features.py"
  steps:
    - >-
      Implement target exactly: Dam x daily issue; water level m at day t+7; optional
      storage mcm separately; labels S32/S34 daily history, S33 monthly only for EDA.
    - >-
      Build feature table and feature provenance list from section11. Enforce data gate:
      >=3 years daily observations across >=8 dams, known vertical datum; if only
      monthly archive exists, accumulate daily data and keep seven-day model
      experimental.
    - >-
      Write dated split manifest: Canonical prospective study: collect from 2028-01-17;
      train 2028-01-17..2028-03-28; tune 2028-03-29..2028-04-12; calibrate
      2028-04-13..2028-04-26; locked test 2028-04-27..2028-05-26. Expanding weekly
      folds; service-day and held-out route/station blocks; purge72h for M14, target
      horizon for other models. Dates assume source approval/readiness tasks pass on
      schedule. If delayed, shift the entire manifest before training; never invent
      earlier observations. Operational bias correction needs matched observed truth:
      train on historical data only if original issue-time forecasts exist; otherwise
      use this prospective window and keep raw weather as baseline. If evidence gate
      fails, write blocked evidence and stop this model branch; remaining model tasks
      only test disabled state.
  commands:
    - ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/models/test_m07_features.py -q"
  acceptance:
    command: ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/models/test_m07_features.py -q"
    expected: >-
      Target and lag assertions pass on real labelled fixture; future-data mutation
      rejected; blocked model exports no prediction.
  hours: 3
- id: T131
  title: "Baseline and bounded candidate: Kerala seven-day dam forecast"
  phase: "P3"
  state: "KL"
  depends_on:
    - "T130"
  files:
    - "src/atlas/models/m07.py"
    - "notebooks/models/m07.ipynb"
    - "tests/models/test_m07_fit.py"
  steps:
    - >-
      Fit baseline: Persistence; seasonal naive; Karnataka pooled model without Kerala
      refit. Save predictions on identical fold rows.
    - >-
      Fit candidate: Ridge, SARIMAX, LightGBM quantile; provisional LightGBM with dam
      fixed category. Use section11 search space and maximum30 CPU trials/2h; neural
      jobs use explicit N-card and resume checkpoints.
    - >-
      Save MLflow run, preprocessing, weights and split hashes; training function
      receives only train/tune data, never test. If blocked, preserve no-model manifest.
  commands:
    - ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/models/test_m07_fit.py -q"
  acceptance:
    command: ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/models/test_m07_fit.py -q"
    expected: >-
      Deterministic train smoke test passes; test rows cannot affect fit; all evaluated
      baselines have same target units and rows.
  hours: 3
- id: T132
  title: "Evaluate and publish decision: Kerala seven-day dam forecast"
  phase: "P3"
  state: "KL"
  depends_on:
    - "T131"
  files:
    - "reports/models/m07.md"
    - "models/registry/m07.json"
    - "tests/models/test_m07_gate.py"
  steps:
    - >-
      Evaluate locked test once; report MAE <=0.90x strongest baseline; RMSE; interval
      coverage 75..85%; separate dam scores and peak-period errors.
    - >-
      Inspect failure modes: Unobserved releases, dam-level datum changes, manual report
      errors; flag implausible jumps rather than smoothing floods away. Include source
      coverage, intervals, sliced performance and limits; block non-supported claims.
    - >-
      Export champion predictions/SHAP/intervals only if all gates pass; else publish
      baseline/research-only status. Save model card and retraining rule.
  commands:
    - ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/models/test_m07_gate.py -q"
  acceptance:
    command: ".\\.venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/models/test_m07_gate.py -q"
    expected: >-
      Release manifest verifies source/split hashes and gate decision; failing model
      remains disabled; report never substitutes targets for achieved scores.
  hours: 3
